-- Old-site (.html) URLs that showed "page not found" on the live site,
-- found by testing every known old URL against maldivestour.guide on
-- 2026-11-26 (lists: data/maldives/migration/redirect-map.json,
-- retired-urls.json, accommodations-v2/resolved-properties.json):
--
-- 1. ~139 old resort/hotel pages (/resorts/<Name>/<Name>.html): the
--    earlier stays redirects (20250123000400) matched by resort title and
--    never took effect on the live database. Now pointed straight at each
--    resort's current Stays page.
-- 2. ~350 old room/tour booking-form pages: sent to the resort, tour or
--    topic page they belonged to (they were left as 404s before).
-- 3. Old partner sign-up pages -> /become-a-partner/.
-- 4. Six existing redirects whose target had moved or was wrong.
--
-- Every target was checked to return 200 live (not a redirect) before
-- this file was written. Cart/checkout/email-template pages with no
-- matching content are deliberately left as 404s.
-- Upserts, so re-running is safe and also re-activates any inactive row.

on conflict (source_path) do update set target_type = excluded.target_type, target_path = excluded.target_path,
  status_code = excluded.status_code, is_active = excluded.is_active, notes = excluded.notes, updated_at = now();
